<%# Device showcase — "here is the app on your screens".

    locals:
      desktop  — image path or url for the laptop screen (optional)
      mobile   — image path or url for the phone screen (optional)
      caption  — optional line rendered over the band

    Rebuilt from BRGEN_OLD's static_pages/intro.html.erb, which did this with two
    photographs — device_macbook_pro.png at 75% width and device_iphone_6.png
    absolutely positioned over it — in a 330px band with a #eee hairline. The
    composition was good and is kept: a wide screen centred, a phone overlapping
    its lower right, the pair cropped by the band so they read as a scene rather
    than as two pictures.

    The photographs are not kept. They are a 2014 MacBook Pro and an iPhone 6,
    and a photographic bezel cannot follow the palette — it is a fixed grey
    object on a surface whose background, ink and border are all tokens. Drawn in
    CSS instead: flat outlines in currentColor, no gradient, no shadow, no
    rounded-glass suggestion, which is the same treatment the rest of this system
    uses and costs no image request.

    Both screens are optional. With no image the frame renders empty and still
    reads as a device, which is what you want on a page whose screenshots have
    not been taken yet. %>
<% desktop = local_assigns[:desktop] %>
<% mobile = local_assigns[:mobile] %>
<% caption = local_assigns[:caption] %>

<div class="device-showcase" role="img"
     aria-label="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:alt, t("showcase.devices", default: "The app on desktop and mobile")) %>">
  <div class="device device--desktop">
    <div class="device-screen">
      <% if desktop %>
        <%# reserved: container — .device--desktop is a 16/10 aspect frame %>
        <%= image_tag desktop, alt: "", loading: "lazy" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <%# The foot is what makes an outlined rectangle read as a laptop. %>
    <div class="device-foot" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="device device--mobile">
    <div class="device-screen">
      <% if mobile %>
        <%# reserved: container — .device--mobile is an aspect frame %>
        <%= image_tag mobile, alt: "", loading: "lazy" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% if caption %>
    <p class="device-showcase-caption"><%= caption %></p>
  <% end %>
</div>
